{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Knm2ceokMtCfnYL8h7uBe3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RoExywBBXfQbKugb3Jp8kM","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C03\\KP-01.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2620,"cache_read_input_tokens":32914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2620},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a84c7db-e2bc-4d04-8952-637ff4edf9ad","uuid":"b22bebec-1148-4a9b-ad41-cb5b197f28db"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RoExywBBXfQbKugb3Jp8kM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS PENERANGAN / INFORMATION SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C03/KP(1/6)\n4\t**Competency Unit:** C03 — Manual Body Massage\n5\t**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Manual Body Massage Consultation\n6\t**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** WHITE / PUTIH\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Objectives (Objektif)\n11\t1. Explain the consultation process specific to manual body massage.\n12\t2. Identify contraindications for manual body massage.\n13\t3. Describe the informed consent requirements for massage services.\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## 1.0 Massage Consultation\n18\t\n19\tBuilding on C01 body consultation, the massage consultation additionally determines:\n20\t- Client's primary reason for massage (relaxation, pain relief, circulation improvement, muscle tension release, cellulite reduction)\n21\t- Areas of concern / pain points\n22\t- Pressure preference (light, medium, firm)\n23\t- Previous massage experience and preferences\n24\t- Specific muscle or joint conditions\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## 2.0 Contraindications for Manual Body Massage\n29\t\n30\t> **AMARAN / WARNING:** NEVER proceed with massage if any absolute contraindication is present. For relative contraindications, obtain written GP/specialist clearance where stated and document on the consultation card before commencing treatment.\n31\t\n32\tContraindications are classified as **systemic** (whole-body; massage must not proceed) or **local** (specific area; massage may proceed but must avoid the site).\n33\t\n34\t### 2.1 Absolute Contraindications (Systemic — No Treatment)\n35\t| Condition | Reason |\n36\t|-----------|--------|\n37\t| Fever / acute infection (*demam / jangkitan akut*) | Risk of spreading infection; body under systemic stress |\n38\t| Contagious skin conditions (*penyakit kulit berjangkit*) | Cross-contamination risk to therapist and other clients |\n39\t| Thrombosis / DVT (*trombosis / trombosis urat dalam*) | Risk of dislodging clot → pulmonary embolism |\n40\t| Cancer / malignancy (without oncologist clearance) | Risk of aiding metastatic spread via lymph stimulation |\n41\t| Recent fractures / sprains (acute stage < 72 hrs) | Risk of further tissue damage |\n42\t| Severe osteoporosis (*osteoporosis teruk*) | Pathological fracture risk under pressure |\n43\t| Acute inflammation / swelling (*keradangan akut*) | Massage increases prostaglandin release; exacerbates condition |\n44\t| Alcohol or drug intoxication (*mabuk alkohol / dadah*) | Impaired pain perception; consent not valid |\n45\t| Anti-coagulant medication (e.g. warfarin, heparin) | Elevated bruising and internal bleeding risk |\n46\t| Acute mental health crisis / psychosis | Inability to give valid consent; unpredictable response |\n47\t\n48\t### 2.2 Local Contraindications (Avoid Area Only)\n49\t| Condition | Action |\n50\t|-----------|--------|\n51\t| Open wounds / burns | Do not massage over affected area |\n52\t| Varicose veins (*varikos vena*) | Avoid direct pressure; work proximal and distal only |\n53\t| Undiagnosed lumps / swellings | Avoid until medically cleared |\n54\t| Bruising (*lebam*) | Avoid bruised area; work surrounding tissue gently |\n55\t| Recent scar tissue (< 6 weeks) | Avoid until scar is fully closed |\n56\t\n57\t### 2.3 Relative Contraindications (Proceed with Caution)\n58\t| Condition | Action |\n59\t|-----------|--------|\n60\t| Pregnancy (*hamil*) | Avoid abdomen in first trimester; use side-lying position; GP approval required |\n61\t| Diabetes (*kencing manis*) | Monitor skin response; reduce pressure; check for neuropathy |\n62\t| Epilepsy (controlled) | Proceed with caution; avoid tapotement; have emergency plan |\n63\t| High/low blood pressure (*tekanan darah tinggi/rendah*) | Monitor; slow gentle movements; avoid sudden position changes |\n64\t| Skin conditions (eczema, psoriasis) | Avoid affected areas; use hypoallergenic medium |\n65\t| Recent surgery (> 6 weeks post-op) | Avoid surgical area; require GP clearance |\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## 3.0 Informed Consent\n70\t\n71\tThe consent process must include:\n72\t- Explanation of the massage procedure and areas to be treated\n73\t- Expected benefits and possible after-effects (soreness, increased urination)\n74\t- Client's right to stop treatment at any time\n75\t- Confirmation of pressure preference\n76\t- Written consent with signature\n77\t\n78\t---\n79\t\n80\t## 4.0 Recording Consultation Findings\n81\t\n82\tUpdate client consultation card with:\n83\t- Massage-specific concerns and goals\n84\t- Pressure preference noted\n85\t- Contraindications reviewed\n86\t- Areas to avoid\n87\t- Consent obtained (date and signature)\n88\t\n89\t---\n90\t\n91\t## References\n92\t1. NOSS S960-002-3:2020 — Manual Body Massage (CoCU C03, WA 1)\n93\t2. Salvo, S.G. (2019). *Massage Therapy: Principles and Practice* (6th ed.). Elsevier.\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a84c7db-e2bc-4d04-8952-637ff4edf9ad","uuid":"a9b8775c-2632-4943-a189-422803255c64","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:54:51.088Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C03\\KP-01.md","content":"# KERTAS PENERANGAN / INFORMATION SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C03/KP(1/6)\n**Competency Unit:** C03 — Manual Body Massage\n**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Manual Body Massage Consultation\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** WHITE / PUTIH\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n1. Explain the consultation process specific to manual body massage.\n2. Identify contraindications for manual body massage.\n3. Describe the informed consent requirements for massage services.\n\n---\n\n## 1.0 Massage Consultation\n\nBuilding on C01 body consultation, the massage consultation additionally determines:\n- Client's primary reason for massage (relaxation, pain relief, circulation improvement, muscle tension release, cellulite reduction)\n- Areas of concern / pain points\n- Pressure preference (light, medium, firm)\n- Previous massage experience and preferences\n- Specific muscle or joint conditions\n\n---\n\n## 2.0 Contraindications for Manual Body Massage\n\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** NEVER proceed with massage if any absolute contraindication is present. For relative contraindications, obtain written GP/specialist clearance where stated and document on the consultation card before commencing treatment.\n\nContraindications are classified as **systemic** (whole-body; massage must not proceed) or **local** (specific area; massage may proceed but must avoid the site).\n\n### 2.1 Absolute Contraindications (Systemic — No Treatment)\n| Condition | Reason |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Fever / acute infection (*demam / jangkitan akut*) | Risk of spreading infection; body under systemic stress |\n| Contagious skin conditions (*penyakit kulit berjangkit*) | Cross-contamination risk to therapist and other clients |\n| Thrombosis / DVT (*trombosis / trombosis urat dalam*) | Risk of dislodging clot → pulmonary embolism |\n| Cancer / malignancy (without oncologist clearance) | Risk of aiding metastatic spread via lymph stimulation |\n| Recent fractures / sprains (acute stage < 72 hrs) | Risk of further tissue damage |\n| Severe osteoporosis (*osteoporosis teruk*) | Pathological fracture risk under pressure |\n| Acute inflammation / swelling (*keradangan akut*) | Massage increases prostaglandin release; exacerbates condition |\n| Alcohol or drug intoxication (*mabuk alkohol / dadah*) | Impaired pain perception; consent not valid |\n| Anti-coagulant medication (e.g. warfarin, heparin) | Elevated bruising and internal bleeding risk |\n| Acute mental health crisis / psychosis | Inability to give valid consent; unpredictable response |\n\n### 2.2 Local Contraindications (Avoid Area Only)\n| Condition | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Open wounds / burns | Do not massage over affected area |\n| Varicose veins (*varikos vena*) | Avoid direct pressure; work proximal and distal only |\n| Undiagnosed lumps / swellings | Avoid until medically cleared |\n| Bruising (*lebam*) | Avoid bruised area; work surrounding tissue gently |\n| Recent scar tissue (< 6 weeks) | Avoid until scar is fully closed |\n\n### 2.3 Relative Contraindications (Proceed with Caution)\n| Condition | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Pregnancy (*hamil*) | Avoid abdomen in first trimester; use side-lying position; GP approval required |\n| Diabetes (*kencing manis*) | Monitor skin response; reduce pressure; check for neuropathy |\n| Epilepsy (controlled) | Proceed with caution; avoid tapotement; have emergency plan |\n| High/low blood pressure (*tekanan darah tinggi/rendah*) | Monitor; slow gentle movements; avoid sudden position changes |\n| Skin conditions (eczema, psoriasis) | Avoid affected areas; use hypoallergenic medium |\n| Recent surgery (> 6 weeks post-op) | Avoid surgical area; require GP clearance |\n\n---\n\n## 3.0 Informed Consent\n\nThe consent process must include:\n- Explanation of the massage procedure and areas to be treated\n- Expected benefits and possible after-effects (soreness, increased urination)\n- Client's right to stop treatment at any time\n- Confirmation of pressure preference\n- Written consent with signature\n\n---\n\n## 4.0 Recording Consultation Findings\n\nUpdate client consultation card with:\n- Massage-specific concerns and goals\n- Pressure preference noted\n- Contraindications reviewed\n- Areas to avoid\n- Consent obtained (date and signature)\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. NOSS S960-002-3:2020 — Manual Body Massage (CoCU C03, WA 1)\n2. Salvo, S.G. (2019). *Massage Therapy: Principles and Practice* (6th ed.). Elsevier.\n","numLines":94,"startLine":1,"totalLines":94}}}
